  "version": 11,
  "description": "Independence rules. Everything is a { value, label } pair: value is the stable key used by logic and stored data and never changes; label is the text people see and can be renamed freely. Treatments and relationships are defined once below and rules refer to them by value. Close affiliates carry one relationship per tree relationship (CA - Ultimate Parent and so on), so each can be treated differently. A relationship's phrase is the plain-language wording used in the independence decision. Each rule lists entries; each entry is one treatment, the relationships (measured from an audit client) it applies to, and exemptServiceLines: the service lines that are exempt from that treatment for those relationships (it can be empty). A relationship appears in at most one entry per rule. The wizard embeds a copy of this file (without the prose fields) and reads rules, labels and relationships from it; exemptServiceLines is defined here but not yet read by the wizard, so its embedded copy has not been updated for it.",

