  "serviceLinesNote": "exemptServiceLines lists, by value from the serviceLines catalog below, the service lines that the treatment does not apply to for that entry. It can be empty, which means no service line is exempt. A value ending in * is a prefix match, so \"TAX*\" is every TAX- service line. For a relationship and service line, the entry that lists the relationship decides: an exempt service line gets no treatment (it is not restricted and needs no materiality check), and any other service line gets the entry's treatment. A relationship with no entry is out of scope. Because a relationship appears in only one entry per rule, use separate entries of the same treatment to give different relationships different exemptions. The wizard does not ask for a service line yet.",

